questions.question:
In a titration of a base with a standard acid:
1. a burette was rinsed with water and then filled with the standard acid;
2. a pipette was rinsed with some base solution;
3. a conical flask was rinsed with some base solution;
4. the pipette transferred a measured volume of base into the flask;
5. indicator was added and the base titrated with the acid.

Which statement is correct?

questions.answer:
**Prop-2-en-1-ol > propanal > butane.**

All have a molar mass of about 58 g mol$^{-1}$, so differences come from the type of intermolecular force:

- prop-2-en-1-ol has an O–H group and forms hydrogen bonds (strongest);
- propanal has a polar C=O, giving dipole–dipole forces;
- butane is non-polar, with only dispersion forces (weakest).

Stronger forces need more energy to overcome, so a higher boiling point.
